  "explanation": "Feature 237 FR-010 makes shapely load on first use instead of at import, so the FIRST seed of a process now pays that import inside its timed region. Measured directly: importing shapely.geometry and shapely.ops costs 0.244s, which is the +0.2s seed 4 shows on field and track; seed 4 is the first seed snapshotted. It is ONE-TIME PER PROCESS, not per map - seeds 25, 39 and 47 read +0.0%, -8.0% and -1.4%, and the TOTAL is -1.3% faster across three independent -end bookends (seed 4 +3.6/+1.8/+3.6%, total -1.3/-1.8/-1.3%). The deferral's purpose is memory: shapely plus the numpy it pulls is 16-22 MiB per worker that all ten gate workers paid merely to collect the package. A loader call inside the per-plot functions was considered as the cause and RULED OUT by measurement - making the check an inline sentinel rather than a call left seed 4 unchanged at +3.6%.",
